<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Android 11 and below (android:fullBackupContent).

  An <include> makes the rules a WHITELIST: once one exists, everything not
  named here is excluded. So this single line is the whole policy — the only
  thing Android may copy to the user's Google Drive is one timestamp, the date
  this install began.

  Deliberately absent, and worth naming: the transactions database, Flutter's
  shared preferences blob (every other setting the app owns), and all app
  files. None of a user's financial life leaves the phone, which is what the
  privacy policy promises and what the missing INTERNET permission enforces
  for the app itself.

  Why back up anything at all: the date is what stops a reinstall from handing
  out a second free trial. Android restores it before first launch, so an
  honest reinstall resumes the window it was already in.

  The path must match MainActivity.TRIAL_ANCHOR_PREFS + ".xml".
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <include domain="sharedpref" path="budgetify_trial_anchor.xml" />
</full-backup-content>
